    "q-105399": {
      "dom_id": "step-q105399",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Which of the following functions is continuous on the interval $(-4,-2]?$",
      "worked_solution": "The correct answer is the following.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14262965/assets/d548d825e9c34024581dcd941eb208860a4ebfdee36df0eb5972babd33fc73eb.png)\n\n \n\nIndeed, we have that $h(x)$ is continuous on the open interval $(-4,-2).$ \n\nAdditionally, the function is left-continuous at $x=-2.$  Hence, it is continuous on the interval $(-4,-2].$ \n\nNotice that \n\n- $f(x)$ is not left-continuous at $x=-2.$\n\n- $g(x)$ and $q(x)$ are not continuous at $x=-3$, and so are not continuous on $(-4,-2].$\n\n- $p(x)$ is not continuous at some point that lies inside the interval $(-4,-2).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
